Used here as a real-world example of XTF 2.4 envelope structure
(`<ili:sender>` as a child element rather than a HEADERSECTION attribute,
the model's own elements under a PREFIXED namespace rather than the
default one, `ili:bid`/`ili:tid` namespaced attributes) - complements
`tests/fixtures/xtf/xtf24allerrors/` (default namespace, no `<ili:sender>`)
for `interlis.xtf.parse` unit coverage. No matching `.ili` model is
distributed with this fragment upstream, so it's used for structural
(parse-layer) tests only, not schema-aware validation.
